00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:36.470
There are marshmallows, fried chicken, ribs, maybe some waffles, cornbread muffins, donuts,
有棉花糖、炸鸡、排骨，可能还有些华夫饼、玉米面包松饼、甜甜圈，

315
00:13:36.470 --> 00:13:40.030
lots of soda, mac and cheese, dumplings.
大量的汽水、通心粉奶酪、饺子。

316
00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:43.810
I swear someone has mashed potatoes and gravy on their plate.
我发誓有人盘子里装的是土豆泥和肉汁。

317
00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:49.870
And then Jim has some strawberries on his plate, probably for the chocolate fountain.
然后吉姆的盘子里有一些草莓，大概是用来蘸巧克力喷泉的。

318
00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:52.890
But I was surprised to spot a bit of healthy food.
但我很惊讶地发现了一些健康食品。

319
00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:55.910
Not surprised to see it on John Krasinski's plate, however.
不过，在约翰·卡拉辛斯基的盘子里看到它倒也不奇怪。

320
00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.770
He was such a healthy eater.
他一直是个很注重健康饮食的人。

321
00:13:57.910 --> 00:13:58.410
He was.
确实是。

322
00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:01.730
Jenna, do you know what I remember about this scene?
珍娜，你知道关于这一幕我记得什么吗？

323
00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:02.310
What?
什么？

324
00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:04.470
How funky that cheese got.
那奶酪变得有多怪味。

325
00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:05.270
Yeah.
是啊。

326
00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:06.910
It got real smelly.
它变得特别臭。

327
00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:07.750
Yeah.
是啊。

328
00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:14.050
Kelly shares on the DVD that they could only keep that cheese melted for three hours.
凯莉在DVD花絮里分享说，那种奶酪只能保持融化状态三个小时。

329
00:14:15.070 --> 00:14:18.870
And then it would start to like coagulate or whatever.
之后它就会开始凝固什么的。

330
00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:20.550
It got so gross.
变得特别恶心。

331
00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:25.370
I mean, that really makes me think twice about any cheese fondue fountain.
我是说，这真的让我对任何奶酪火锅喷泉都得三思了。

332
00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:26.870
The fountain food.
喷泉食物。

333
00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:29.050
I might be done with fountain food.
我可能再也不想吃喷泉食物了。

334
00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:34.750
When I was in college, I had a boyfriend and we read that there was like this protein shake
我上大学时，有个男朋友，我们读到有一家蛋白粉公司，

335
00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:41.170
company that was going to give a $10,000 prize to whoever lost the most weight and like gain
承诺给减重最多且通过使用他们的蛋白粉增加最多肌肉的人，

336
00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:44.770
the most muscle by like using their protein shake.
提供一万美元的奖金。

337
00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:45.210
Right.
对。

338
00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:47.430
So the idea is to like get healthy, lose weight.
所以主意就是变得健康、减轻体重。

339
00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:50.090
And here's your incentive is a bunch of money or something.
而给你的激励就是一大笔钱之类的。

340
00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:50.630
Yeah.
是啊。

341
00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:51.810
So we entered.
所以我们就参加了。

342
00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:53.090
You and your boyfriend?
你和你男朋友？

343
00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:53.470
Yeah.
对。

344
00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:55.530
You did the shake challenge?
你们参加了那个奶昔挑战赛？

345
00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:56.290
We did.
我们参加了。

346
00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:57.190
Here's the thing.
重点是。

347
00:14:57.190 --> 00:15:00.850
We did the same thing where like in the week before.
我们也做了同样的事，就在比赛前一周。

348
00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:02.490
You carved up?
你们疯狂进食了？

349
00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:03.050
We did.
没错。

350
00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:04.230
We ate a bunch of food.
我们吃了一大堆东西。

351
00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:06.430
I probably gained about five pounds.
我大概胖了五磅左右。

352
00:15:06.890 --> 00:15:07.790
In one week.
就一周时间。

353
00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:08.170
Yeah.
是啊。

354
00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:13.670
Because we just like ate pizza and burgers because we were like, this is great.
因为我们当时就只吃披萨和汉堡，还觉得这感觉太棒了。

355
00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:17.950
I mean, we'll start out with more weight and then we'll lose it all and more.
我的意思是，我们先增重，然后再把这些体重减掉，甚至减得更多。

356
00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:19.390
And we'll win $10,000.
这样我们就能赢那一万美元了。

357
00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:20.210
Yeah.
是啊。

358
00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:22.150
I mean, we took pictures of ourselves.
我们还给自己拍了照片。

359
00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:23.830
I still have it.
我那儿还有呢。

360
00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:24.550
Oh, no.
噢，不。

361
00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:26.290
I mean, somewhere I have it.
我是说，我肯定在哪儿存着。

362
00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:30.610
I know because I was cleaning out some old photo albums and I found it and it jogged
我知道是因为我当时在清理旧相册，发现了那张照片，然后就勾起了

363
00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:31.110
this memory.
这段回忆。

364
00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:35.870
You had to prove the day, you know, of the weight loss start.
你得证明日期，你知道的，就是减肥开始的那天。

365
00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:36.350
Yeah.
是啊。

366
00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:38.590
So you had to hold up that day's newspaper.
所以你得举着当天的报纸。

367
00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:40.110
I mean, like a hostage photo.
就像那种人质照片一样。

368
00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:41.090
Oh, my God.
天哪。

369
00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:43.050
So I've got this picture of myself.
所以我留着那张自己的照片。

370
00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:45.690
This was before you could Instagram.
那是在还没法用Instagram的时候。

371
00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:48.610
Now you can Instagram and it's a timestamp.
现在你可以发Instagram，上面自带时间戳。

372
00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:50.770
But back then you had to hold up like a newspaper.
但那时候你得举着报纸之类的东西。

373
00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:51.270
Yeah.
是啊。

374
00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:52.970
And take it with a regular old camera.
还得用那种老式相机拍。

375
00:15:53.190 --> 00:15:55.970
I'm in like a sports bra and some like sport shorts.
我当时穿着运动内衣和运动短裤。

376
00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:56.690
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

377
00:15:57.110 --> 00:15:58.550
And I'm holding up a newspaper.
手里举着一份报纸。

378
00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:04.790
And I will tell you what, not only did we not win, I did not lose any of the weight.
我跟你说，我们不仅没赢，我连一磅都没减掉。

379
00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:06.710
That you gained carb loading?
就是你为了“碳水加载”而增重的那次？

380
00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:07.330
That's right.
没错。

381
00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:11.590
After the eight weeks, I mean, we gave up so quickly.
八周之后，我们很快就放弃了。

382
00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:14.210
We were all in for the first week of the fitness challenge.
健身挑战的第一周我们还全力以赴来着。

383
00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:14.610
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

384
00:16:14.710 --> 00:16:20.850
And then all that happened was from all of this is that I gained five pounds and then
结果到头来，我不仅胖了五磅，还

385
00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:22.170
I held up a newspaper.
举着报纸拍了张照。

386
00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:23.970
The end.
完事儿。

387
00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:30.340
So that memory came flooding back as I was watching us in this conference room scene.
所以当我看到我们在会议室的那一幕时，这段记忆就涌上心头了。

388
00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:34.560
So Stanley, Meredith, and Creed have plans for their leftovers.
所以斯坦利、梅雷迪思和克里德打算把剩菜带走。

389
00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:35.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

390
00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:38.180
You know, Stanley really wants to take some of these dumplings home.
你知道，斯坦利真的很想把这些饺子带回家。

391
00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:41.580
But Dwight is like, no, no, you cannot take any of this food home.
但德怀特说，不行，不行，你们不能把这些食物带回家。

392
00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:42.600
We're eating healthy now.
我们现在要吃得健康点。

393
00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:48.120
And he starts spraying what looks like an insect repellent all over all of the food.
然后他开始往所有的食物上喷洒看起来像是杀虫剂的东西。

394
00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:54.000
We had a fan question from Chelsea B, Alice R, and Henry F.
我们收到了来自切尔西·B、爱丽丝·R和亨利·F的粉丝提问。

395
00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:57.980
What was in the bottle that Dwight is spraying on the food?
德怀特喷在食物上的瓶子里装的是什么？

396
00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:00.500
Well, guess who knows?
嗯，猜猜谁知道？

397
00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:01.420
You?
你吗？

398
00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:03.820
Me, thanks to our crew.
是我，多亏了我们的剧组人员。

399
00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:07.040
It was not real bug spray, of course.
那当然不是真的杀虫剂。

400
00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:10.860
This was a prop bottle that Phil Shea had designed.
那是菲尔·谢伊专门设计的道具瓶。

401
00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:12.040
He had this made.
这是他让人特制的。

402
00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:15.140
And it was full of aerosol water.
里面装满了喷雾水。

403
00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:16.220
Oh.
噢。

404
00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:18.120
So he was just spraying water.
所以他只是在喷水。

405
00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:22.040
You know, I assumed that's what it was, but it didn't look like water.
你知道，我本来以为是水，但看起来不像水。

406
00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:23.140
I mean, it looks so real.
我是说，看起来太真实了。

407
00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:24.660
I thought it looked real.
我觉得它看起来很真实。

408
00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:27.540
And I thought everyone's reactions were really good.
而且我觉得大家的反应都非常好。

409
00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:28.980
Great acting, folks.
演得太棒了，各位。

410
00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:29.800
You sold it.
你们演活了。

411
00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:32.340
Well, now the gang is going to go down to the warehouse.
好了，现在大家要下到仓库去了。

412
00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:33.360
They're going to weigh in.
他们要去称体重了。

413
00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:34.220
Yes.
没错。

414
00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:40.400
And Jenna, at one minute, five seconds, there is a great shot of the big scale that we're
还有珍娜，在1分05秒的时候，有一个大秤的特写镜头，

415
00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:41.460
all going to get weighed on.
我们都要在那上面称重。

416
00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:44.080
And I have a prop breakdown.
我有一份道具清单。

417
00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:45.420
Give it to me.
给我看看。

418
00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:45.900
Okay.
好的。

419
00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:50.420
That scale was custom made by Rice Lake Weighing SysteMs.
那个秤是Rice Lake Weighing Systems公司定制的。

420
00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:53.300
They made it specific to our requests.
他们是根据我们的要求专门制作的。

421
00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:58.000
And they were able to program the little computer screen with whatever the writers wanted them
而且他们还能按照编剧的要求，在小电脑屏幕上显示任何内容，

422
00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.000
to put on it, right?
对吧？

423
00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:00.580
It was like part of the joke.
这就像是笑话的一部分。

424
00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:01.160
Our weight.
我们的体重。

425
00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:03.900
That was all like a writer's joke.
那全是编剧的梗。

426
00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:08.560
My mind is being blown right now that that was not a real scale.
我现在简直惊呆了，原来那不是真的秤。

427
00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:10.320
No, the scale didn't exiSt.
不，那个秤本来不存在。

428
00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:11.840
It was made just for us.
它是专门为我们制作的。

429
00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:17.060
And Rice Lake Weighing System didn't ask for any credit or any company plug.
而且Rice Lake Weighing Systems公司没有要求任何署名或植入广告。

430
00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:19.160
They were huge fans of the show.
他们是这部剧的忠实粉丝。

431
00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:22.160
And they did come to set the day we filmed this.
我们拍摄那天他们还来到了片场。

432
00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:24.820
And everyone on our crew said they were so nice.
我们剧组的所有人都说他们人非常好。

433
00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:30.760
And after this episode aired, that scale stayed in the warehouse as part of the warehouse set.
这一集播出后，那个秤就留在了仓库里，作为仓库布景的一部分。

434
00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:31.880
That I remember.
这一点我记得。

435
00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:32.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

436
00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:36.500
Now, during this weigh-in, Angela, what's up with Meredith's face?
现在，在这次称重过程中，安吉拉，梅雷迪思的脸是怎么回事？

437
00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:37.500
Did you notice?
你注意到了吗？

438
00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:38.880
Her face is all red.
她的脸全红了。

439
00:18:38.980 --> 00:18:40.440
We got a lot of mail about it.
我们收到了很多关于此事的来信。

440
00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:42.340
They want to know what's going on.
大家想知道发生了什么。

441
00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:44.680
Was there a storyline that was cut or something?
是有什么剧情被剪掉了吗？

442
00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:45.800
Oh, yes.
噢，是的。

443
00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:51.100
I want you guys to know I took a photo of Kate's face as Meredith looking like that.
我想让你们知道，我拍了一张凯特化着梅雷迪思那种妆容的照片。

444
00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:52.920
And I texted it to Kate last night.
昨晚我发短信给了凯特。

445
00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:54.100
And I said, Kate, you know what?
我说，凯特，你知道吗？

446
00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:58.320
You should win Team Player Award for the run of the office.
你应该获得《办公室》全剧的“最佳团队合作奖”。

447
00:18:58.340 --> 00:19:01.620
Because her character was always getting into some kind of mishap,
因为她的角色总是会遇到各种倒霉事，

448
00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:05.200
which resulted in Kate being in the hair and makeup trailer forever, right?
导致凯特得在化妆间待上好久，对吧？

449
00:19:05.480 --> 00:19:05.580
Yeah.
是的。

450
00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:07.940
And here was the storyline.
这就是当时的剧情。

451
00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:10.140
And it's shared in the deleted scenes.
这部分内容在删减片段里有提到。

452
00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:13.040
Meredith gets severely sunburned.
梅雷迪思被严重晒伤了。

453
00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:15.440
And here is her explanation.
这是她的解释。

454
00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:16.940
Sam, can you play the clip?
萨姆，能放一下那段视频吗？

455
00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:19.720
These guys took me out in the fishing boat.
这些人带我坐渔船出海了。

456
00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:21.300
I don't think I caught anything.
我觉得我什么都没钓到。

457
00:19:22.380 --> 00:19:23.180
Hello, hello.
你好，你好。

458
00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:23.740
Hey.
嘿。

459
00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:26.360
Your face is almost back to normal.
你的脸快恢复正常了。

460
00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:28.240
One more kid calls me Hellboy.
要是再有小孩叫我地狱男爵，

461
00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:29.180
I swear to God.
我发誓。

462
00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:30.020
Oh, you wish.
噢，你想得美。

463
00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:31.420
Hellboy's a hero.
地狱男爵可是个英雄。

464
00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:33.060
Oh, wow.
噢，哇哦。

465
00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:33.560
Yeah.
是啊。

466
00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:36.820
She went out on a boat, got super, super sunburned.
她坐船出海，晒得非常非常严重。

467
00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:41.760
And this was something they had to watch in continuity of which stage of the sunburn was
他们得盯着连续性，看她的脸处于

468
00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:42.480
her face at.
晒伤的哪个阶段。

469
00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:44.560
Then the whole storyline got deleted.
后来整条故事线都被删了。

470
00:19:44.880 --> 00:19:47.980
But they couldn't take out Kate's face.
但他们没法把凯特的脸给删掉。

471
00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:48.700
You know what I mean?
你懂我意思吗？

472
00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:49.100
Yeah.
懂。

473
00:19:49.300 --> 00:19:49.560
Yeah.
是啊。

474
00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:51.180
So they just had to leave it in.
所以他们只能保留那段戏。

475
00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:55.640
And Kate said the day after the show aired, Steve came up to her on set and was like,
凯特说剧集播出后的第二天，史蒂夫在片场走过来对她说，

476
00:19:55.700 --> 00:19:56.280
you know what, Kate?
你知道吗，凯特？

477
00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:57.520
I still thought it was funny.
我还是觉得那很有趣。

478
00:19:57.860 --> 00:20:00.800
You know, I kind of love that Meredith has this mystery about her.
你知道，我挺喜欢梅雷迪思身上那种神秘感的。

479
00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:01.380
Yeah.
是啊。

480
00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:04.580
That she has this whole other life we don't even need to explain.
她有我们根本不需要解释的另一面生活。

481
00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:09.220
And Kate said it made her feel so good that Steve was so thoughtful to come over and say
凯特说史蒂夫能这么贴心地特意过来跟她说这些，

482
00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:09.480
that.
让她感觉非常好。

483
00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:14.360
That was hard when you had a storyline and then you'd watch the episode.
当你拍了故事线，然后看剧集的时候，那种感觉很难受。

484
00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:16.080
They wouldn't warn you a lot of the times.
他们很多时候都不会提前通知你。

485
00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:18.540
You'd just watch the episode and it was gone.
你看着看着剧，发现戏份没了。

486
00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:19.260
Yeah.
是啊。

487
00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:23.480
And you know, with supporting cast, we were often, you know, in the B or C story.
而且你知道，作为配角，我们经常是在B线或C线故事里。

488
00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:25.680
And those really got moved around a lot.
那些故事线确实经常被挪来挪去。

489
00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:26.200
Yeah.
是啊。

490
00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:27.620
And trimmed and edited.
被删减和编辑。

491
00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:28.640
And it did happen.
确实发生过。

492
00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:30.740
But Kate, man, such a good sport.
但凯特，天哪，真是个好脾气的人。

493
00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:31.580
Wow.
哇。

494
00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:37.360
Guys, also in this scene, Michael throws Pam off the scale because she's going to go away
伙计们，这一幕里，迈克尔把帕姆从秤上推开了，因为她要去

495
00:20:37.360 --> 00:20:38.200
to art school.
上艺术学校了。

496
00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:40.460
So he doesn't want her extra poundage.
所以他不想让她增加额外的体重。

497
00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:46.440
Now they've already weighed in and then Pam gets off the scale and a new weight is displayed.
他们已经称过重了，然后帕姆从秤上下来，显示出了一个新的体重。

498
00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:47.500
So embarrassing.
太尴尬了。

499
00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:50.960
Everyone's number change.
每个人的数字都变了。

500
00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:51.520
Yeah.
是啊。

501
00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:57.440
We got some fan mail from Kim C who said, during the group weigh-in, it becomes clear that Pam
我们收到了一封来自Kim C的粉丝来信，她说在集体称重时，很明显Pam

502
00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:59.460
weighs 126 pounds.
体重是126磅。

503
00:21:00.100 --> 00:21:05.080
Jenna, did the writers consult you about your actual weight when they added this fact?
Jenna，编剧在加入这个事实时，有没有就你的真实体重咨询过你？

504
00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:08.180
Or did they just guess how much they thought you might weigh?
还是他们只是猜测了他们认为你可能有的体重？

505
00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:12.420
And were you comfortable with sharing this speculation about your weight?
对于分享这种关于你体重的猜测，你感到自在吗？

506
00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:13.820
Well, I'll tell you guys.
嗯，我告诉你们吧。

507
00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:20.020
Actually, in the script, the original table draft, Pam weighed 145 pounds.
其实在剧本的初稿里，Pam的体重是145磅。

508
00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:20.660
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

509
00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:27.780
And I said, you guys, this is, I feel like a weird thing for me to split hairs about, but
我说，伙计们，我觉得为了这个去斤斤计较有点奇怪，但是

510
00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:30.220
I don't weigh 145 pounds.
我没有145磅。

511
00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:30.740
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

512
00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:31.740
It's not accurate.
这不准确。

513
00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:37.480
Why don't you just put my real weight, which at the time was 126 pounds.
你们为什么不直接写我的真实体重呢，当时是126磅。

514
00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:40.620
I don't weigh 126 pounds anymore.
我现在已经不是126磅了。

515
00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:41.160
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

516
00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:42.660
But at the time, that was my weight.
但在当时，那就是我的体重。

517
00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:44.460
And so they changed it.
所以他们就改了。

518
00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:44.980
Yeah.
是啊。

519
00:21:45.160 --> 00:21:49.040
But yeah, when they speculated about my weight, they put me at 145.
不过确实，当他们猜测我的体重时，他们写的是145磅。

520
00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:51.800
And I just, I don't know, I just corrected it.
我只是，我不知道，我就是纠正了一下。

521
00:21:51.860 --> 00:21:53.320
I thought it should be correct.
我觉得应该准确一点。

522
00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:54.680
I have no problem with that.
我对此没什么意见。

523
00:21:54.920 --> 00:21:59.020
Well, Jenna, that scene made me laugh just because your performance, your reaction, you
Jenna，那场戏让我发笑，纯粹是因为你的表演，你的反应，你

524
00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:01.900
watch everyone doing the math and you're just standing there.
看着每个人都在算数，而你就站在那里。

525
00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:02.140
Yeah.
是啊。

526
00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:06.000
And it was very funny the way you played that moment.
你处理那个瞬间的方式非常有趣。

527
00:22:06.520 --> 00:22:09.220
Now it's week two of their weight loss conteSt.
现在是他们减肥比赛的第二周。

528
00:22:09.620 --> 00:22:10.660
Oscar and Andy arrive.
Oscar和Andy到了。

529
00:22:10.820 --> 00:22:12.200
They're going to hold the elevator for Stanley.
他们打算给Stanley留电梯。

530
00:22:12.420 --> 00:22:14.020
And Stanley says he forgot something.
然后Stanley说他忘了点东西。

531
00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:15.300
And then he takes the stairs.
接着他就去走楼梯了。

532
00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:15.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

533
00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:16.720
Without them knowing.
在他们不知情的情况下。

534
00:22:17.020 --> 00:22:21.840
And he has a great talking head where he shares that he's been losing weight on his own.
他有一个很棒的采访镜头，分享了他一直在自己减肥。

535
00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:26.640
And he just noticed some of his speed and fire, that he's lost a little bit of his pick up and go.
他注意到自己失去了一些活力和干劲，失去了一点那种雷厉风行的劲头。

536
00:22:26.800 --> 00:22:28.380
And he's doing this for himself.
他这么做是为了他自己。

537
00:22:28.720 --> 00:22:29.160
Yes.
是的。

538
00:22:29.440 --> 00:22:33.000
And in this talking head, he shows an old photo of himself.
在那个采访镜头里，他展示了一张他自己的旧照片。

539
00:22:33.640 --> 00:22:34.040
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

540
00:22:34.220 --> 00:22:35.840
Well, we got some mail about that.
嗯，我们收到了一些关于那张照片的来信。

541
00:22:36.020 --> 00:22:38.420
People wanted to know, what is this picture?
大家想知道，这张照片是什么？

542
00:22:38.680 --> 00:22:41.080
Is this from Leslie, David Baker's real life?
这是Leslie，也就是David Baker现实生活中的照片吗？

543
00:22:41.080 --> 00:22:41.280
Yes.
是的。

544
00:22:41.280 --> 00:22:43.140
Is this young Leslie in this photo?
照片里是年轻时的Leslie吗？

545
00:22:43.480 --> 00:22:45.540
It is young Leslie in the photo.
照片里确实是年轻时的Leslie。

546
00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:46.620
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

547
00:22:46.620 --> 00:22:49.620
I texted Leslie, and he gave me all the info.
我给Leslie发了短信，他给了我所有信息。

548
00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:50.780
Oh, let's hear it.
哦，快说来听听。

549
00:22:50.940 --> 00:22:52.420
It's a Photoshop picture.
那是一张PS过的照片。

550
00:22:52.420 --> 00:22:55.160
He does not know any of the other people in the picture.
他不认识照片里的任何其他人。

551
00:22:55.380 --> 00:22:55.700
Got it.
明白了。

552
00:22:55.800 --> 00:23:00.460
They Photoshopped him into it using one of his old prom photos.
他们用他以前的一张毕业舞会照片把他P进去了。

553
00:23:00.880 --> 00:23:01.860
Oh, Leslie.
噢，莱斯利。

554
00:23:02.240 --> 00:23:03.700
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

555
00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:04.120
Yeah.
是啊。

556
00:23:04.540 --> 00:23:07.980
Well, they're really taking this whole get healthy fitness thing seriously.
好吧，他们真的很认真地对待这次健身活动。

557
00:23:08.240 --> 00:23:10.900
Holly is running a yoga class in the conference room.
霍莉正在会议室里开瑜伽课。

558
00:23:11.040 --> 00:23:13.080
I only saw three people in attendance.
我只看到有三个人参加。

559
00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:14.480
Creed, Kelly, and Michael.
克里德、凯利和迈克尔。

560
00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:16.020
I didn't see anyone else.
我没看到其他人。

561
00:23:16.020 --> 00:23:16.560
Oh.
噢。

562
00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:17.340
Yeah.
是啊。

563
00:23:17.840 --> 00:23:19.940
And then Michael is so excited.
然后迈克尔特别兴奋。

564
00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:24.780
He runs up to Jim as Jim is going into the bathroom and is like, did you see Holly's butt?
吉姆去洗手间的时候，他跑过去问，你看到霍莉的屁股了吗？

565
00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:25.760
And Jim's like, no.
吉姆说，没有。

566
00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:26.700
You know why?
你知道为什么吗？

567
00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:27.800
Because we don't do that.
因为我们不那样做。

568
00:23:28.080 --> 00:23:30.100
Friends don't talk about other friends' butts, right?
朋友之间不会谈论彼此的屁股，对吧？

569
00:23:30.500 --> 00:23:35.520
And Jim is really trying to get Michael to have a little growth, right?
吉姆真的在努力让迈克尔有所成长，对吧？

570
00:23:35.700 --> 00:23:35.860
Yep.
没错。

571
00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:37.940
And he's like, what have you learned about her?
他问，你对她有什么了解？

572
00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:42.000
And Michael says, I learned that she broke her left leg twice in one year.
迈克尔说，我知道她一年内摔断了两次左腿。

573
00:23:42.180 --> 00:23:44.600
I learned that she's allergic to sesame seeds.
我知道她对芝麻过敏。

574
00:23:44.600 --> 00:23:50.500
I learned that she has read Lonesome Dove three times and that her butt refuses to quit,
我知道她读过三遍《寂寞之鸽》，而且她的屁股真是绝了，

575
00:23:50.660 --> 00:23:50.980
you know?
你知道吗？

576
00:23:51.200 --> 00:23:52.240
And Jim's like, I give up.
吉姆就觉得，我放弃了。

577
00:23:52.580 --> 00:23:54.180
Little sidebar moment for you.
给你讲个小插曲。

578
00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:55.140
What's that?
什么？

579
00:23:55.140 --> 00:24:00.480
Lonesome Dove was written by Larry McMurtry, who is from my hometown of Archer City, Texas.
《寂寞之鸽》是拉里·麦克穆特里写的，他是我德克萨斯州阿彻城的同乡。

580
00:24:00.840 --> 00:24:01.280
Yes.
是的。

581
00:24:01.540 --> 00:24:03.480
And I knew Larry and I know his family.
我认识拉里，也认识他的家人。

582
00:24:03.900 --> 00:24:06.280
And Larry was this amazing, prolific writer.
拉里是一位了不起的多产作家。

583
00:24:06.520 --> 00:24:12.700
I got so excited just to see one of his pieces of work mentioned on The Office, knowing that I grew up going to his bookstore.
能在《办公室》里提到他的作品，我太激动了，因为我从小就是去他的书店长大的。

584
00:24:12.700 --> 00:24:13.860
That is so cool.
那太酷了。

585
00:24:14.140 --> 00:24:14.680
Love it.
真棒。

586
00:24:14.820 --> 00:24:18.600
You guys got to know, there's only like 1,800 people in Archer City, so everybody knows everybody.
你们得知道，阿彻城只有大约1800人，所以大家都认识彼此。

587
00:24:18.920 --> 00:24:20.900
We got some fan mail from Brittany.
我们收到了布列塔尼寄来的一封粉丝来信。

588
00:24:21.240 --> 00:24:21.660
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

589
00:24:21.860 --> 00:24:27.880
She did her own little mini deep dive on sesame seed allergies.
她自己对芝麻过敏做了一次小小的深度研究。

590
00:24:28.440 --> 00:24:28.960
Oh.
噢。

591
00:24:29.360 --> 00:24:29.680
Yeah.
是啊。

592
00:24:29.840 --> 00:24:31.000
She did a deep dive?
她做了深度研究？

593
00:24:31.040 --> 00:24:31.660
She did.
是的。

594
00:24:31.860 --> 00:24:39.000
She said that she would like us to know that sesame seed allergies are actually the ninth most common type of food allergy.
她说她想让我们知道，芝麻过敏实际上是第九大最常见的食物过敏。

595
00:24:39.260 --> 00:24:40.420
I did not know that.
我以前不知道。

596
00:24:40.680 --> 00:24:42.020
Do you have any allergies?
你有什么过敏吗？

597
00:24:42.020 --> 00:24:42.940
I do.
我有。

598
00:24:43.120 --> 00:24:44.420
I'm allergic to sweet potatoes.
我对红薯过敏。

599
00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:45.480
Crazy.
太疯狂了。

600
00:24:45.900 --> 00:24:46.280
Yeah.
是啊。

601
00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:53.100
I found that out late in life because my mom would only make sweet potatoes at Thanksgiving.
我直到人生后期才发现这一点，因为我妈只在感恩节做红薯。

602
00:24:53.420 --> 00:24:57.780
And I'm sorry, mom, but they always looked really gross to me, so I just never even ate them.
抱歉了妈，但它们在我看来一直都很恶心，所以我从来没吃过。

603
00:24:57.880 --> 00:25:02.500
I don't know if I had some sort of like visceral kind of instinct that I shouldn't eat them.
我不知道自己是不是有一种本能，觉得我不该吃它们。

604
00:25:02.500 --> 00:25:02.780
Like your body knew?
就像你的身体知道一样？

605
00:25:03.380 --> 00:25:03.800
Yeah.
没错。

606
00:25:04.040 --> 00:25:05.620
But I never ate them.
但我确实从来没吃过。

607
00:25:05.840 --> 00:25:09.480
And then my first Thanksgiving in Los Angeles, I couldn't go home.
后来我在洛杉矶过的第一个感恩节，我没能回家。

608
00:25:09.540 --> 00:25:10.380
I couldn't afford it.
我负担不起路费。

609
00:25:10.380 --> 00:25:17.060
So me and my friends, we had our own Thanksgiving, and someone brought some sweet potatoes that looked effing amazing.
所以我和朋友们自己过了感恩节，有人带了一些看起来超级棒的红薯来。

610
00:25:17.640 --> 00:25:19.080
So I had some.
于是我吃了一些。

611
00:25:19.240 --> 00:25:21.160
The next day, I got super sick.
第二天，我病得非常厉害。

612
00:25:21.440 --> 00:25:22.680
I wrote it off.
我没当回事。

613
00:25:22.680 --> 00:25:25.520
I had taken some of those sweet potatoes home as a leftover.
我把剩下的一些红薯带回了家。

614
00:25:25.960 --> 00:25:28.560
I ate them again, got super sick again.
我又吃了一次，结果又病得很厉害。

615
00:25:28.940 --> 00:25:32.200
That's when the doctor was like, I think you should stop eating sweet potatoes.
那时候医生就说，我觉得你应该停止吃红薯了。

616
00:25:32.640 --> 00:25:36.660
I got an allergy test, and I am allergic to sweet potatoes.
我做了过敏测试，结果我对红薯过敏。

617
00:25:36.660 --> 00:25:44.820
My daughter has a mild allergy to dairy, but you can really tell like if she's had, you know, ice cream and stuff, she'll get really stuffy.
我女儿对乳制品有轻微过敏，但你真的能看出来，如果她吃了冰淇淋之类的东西，她就会变得鼻塞。

618
00:25:45.280 --> 00:25:46.120
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

619
00:25:46.420 --> 00:25:46.740
Yeah.
没错。

620
00:25:47.080 --> 00:25:52.080
A lot of people have like a lactose intolerance that causes like some kind of like diarrhea.
很多人有乳糖不耐受，会导致某种程度的腹泻。

621
00:25:52.080 --> 00:25:54.740
Well, this is our spinoff podcaSt.
好吧，这是我们的衍生播客。

622
00:25:54.800 --> 00:25:55.720
It's called.
名字叫。

623
00:25:56.680 --> 00:25:57.940
What Food Studio?
什么食物工作室？

624
00:25:58.200 --> 00:26:00.060
Body Fluids and Other Stories.
体液与其他故事。

625
00:26:00.460 --> 00:26:06.460
I mean, since we're on the subject of milk and stuff, I just want to say, guys, don't give milk to cats.
我是说，既然我们聊到了牛奶之类的话题，我只想说，伙计们，别给猫喂牛奶。

626
00:26:06.820 --> 00:26:07.300
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

627
00:26:07.380 --> 00:26:08.420
It makes them sick.
那会让它们生病。

628
00:26:08.640 --> 00:26:08.920
Yeah.
是啊。

629
00:26:09.080 --> 00:26:12.700
It's like a thing that's been passed down in these cartoons forever.
这就像是动画片里流传已久的事情。

630
00:26:12.700 --> 00:26:14.480
You give cats a dish of milk.
你给猫一碟牛奶。

631
00:26:14.660 --> 00:26:18.000
They are allergic to the dairy and milk.
它们对乳制品和牛奶过敏。

632
00:26:18.180 --> 00:26:18.760
Don't give it to them.
别喂给它们。

633
00:26:19.180 --> 00:26:20.960
Can I add to your milk with cats thing?
我能补充一下你关于猫和牛奶的说法吗？

634
00:26:21.160 --> 00:26:21.500
Oh, yeah.
哦，当然。

635
00:26:21.680 --> 00:26:22.660
Don't give bread to ducks.
别给鸭子喂面包。

636
00:26:23.320 --> 00:26:24.780
Oh, bread to ducks.
哦，给鸭子喂面包。

637
00:26:25.020 --> 00:26:26.280
You know what you can give them?
你知道能喂它们什么吗？

638
00:26:26.620 --> 00:26:26.900
What?
什么？

639
00:26:27.080 --> 00:26:27.520
Peas.
豌豆。

640
00:26:27.900 --> 00:26:28.540
Oh, peas.
哦，豌豆。

641
00:26:28.640 --> 00:26:29.100
And bird seed.
还有鸟食。

642
00:26:29.620 --> 00:26:29.880
Okay.
好的。

643
00:26:30.820 --> 00:26:32.300
