00:33:31.960 --> 00:33:34.900
which I thought was pretty ballsy for the documentary crew.
我觉得这对纪录片摄制组来说挺大胆的。

806
00:33:35.080 --> 00:33:37.280
Well, they need to follow up on these things.
嗯，他们需要跟进这些事情。

807
00:33:38.200 --> 00:33:43.800
Now we have a scene where Michael, through his window, sees that Pam is getting into her
现在我们看到迈克尔通过窗户看到帕姆正在上车，

808
00:33:43.800 --> 00:33:49.780
car, she's getting ready to drive to Pratt, and he has not said his goodbye.
她准备开车去普拉特学院，而他还没跟她道别。

809
00:33:50.120 --> 00:33:51.420
No, he hasn't.
没错，他还没道别。

810
00:33:51.520 --> 00:33:55.800
And I want you to know, I know whose office it was that he was in.
我想让你知道，我知道他当时是在谁的办公室里。

811
00:33:56.020 --> 00:33:57.180
Was it Paul Lieberstein's?
是保罗·利伯斯坦的吗？

812
00:33:57.260 --> 00:33:58.760
No, it was Jen Salatus.
不，是简·萨拉图斯的。

813
00:33:58.980 --> 00:33:59.260
Okay.
好吧。

814
00:33:59.620 --> 00:34:00.180
There you go.
原来如此。

815
00:34:00.180 --> 00:34:03.700
If you're curious, that's the writer's room that Michael was in.
如果你好奇的话，迈克尔当时就在编剧室里。

816
00:34:03.940 --> 00:34:09.480
And poor Michael, he practically wipes out two flights of stairs trying to get to Pam
可怜的迈克尔，他为了赶去跟帕姆道别，差点在两层楼梯上摔个底朝天。

817
00:34:09.480 --> 00:34:10.920
so he could say goodbye.
这太搞笑了。

818
00:34:11.240 --> 00:34:11.960
It's so funny.
这太搞笑了。

819
00:34:11.960 --> 00:34:14.520
And he wrote her a poem, but he left it upstairs.
他还给她写了一首诗，但落在了楼上。

820
00:34:14.680 --> 00:34:17.080
It ends with the word seagulls.
结尾用的是“海鸥”这个词。

821
00:34:17.420 --> 00:34:19.400
Here's what I have to say about this scene.
关于这场戏，我想说的是：

822
00:34:19.600 --> 00:34:22.960
Pam is going to drive to New York in a pencil skirt.
帕姆要穿着铅笔裙开车去纽约。

823
00:34:23.280 --> 00:34:25.200
Also, here was my question.
另外，我有个疑问。

824
00:34:25.200 --> 00:34:26.860
Where's she going to park her car?
她要把车停在哪儿？

825
00:34:27.280 --> 00:34:29.320
There's nowhere to park your car in New York City.
纽约市根本没地方停车。

826
00:34:29.460 --> 00:34:30.940
You have to pay for a parking spot.
你得花钱租停车位。

827
00:34:31.060 --> 00:34:31.960
Well, she's going to Brooklyn.
嗯，她是去布鲁克林。

828
00:34:32.340 --> 00:34:33.700
She's going to like a college campus.
她是去大学校园之类的地方。

829
00:34:33.960 --> 00:34:35.100
You think they have a spot for her?
你觉得他们会给她留个车位吗？

830
00:34:35.280 --> 00:34:36.060
I think they do.
我觉得会有。

831
00:34:36.240 --> 00:34:36.880
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

832
00:34:37.040 --> 00:34:38.280
I think there's a campus parking lot.
我想应该有校园停车场。

833
00:34:38.280 --> 00:34:38.940
Okay, okay, okay.
好吧，好吧，好吧。

834
00:34:39.140 --> 00:34:40.540
I'm not worried about that.
我不担心那个。

835
00:34:40.680 --> 00:34:44.480
I'm worried about why did she come into work even for a half day?
我担心的是她为什么还要来上半天班？

836
00:34:44.740 --> 00:34:46.400
Why didn't she change her clothes?
她为什么不换身衣服？

837
00:34:46.400 --> 00:34:51.600
She's going to arrive at Pratt in a pencil skirt and pantyhose.
她要穿着铅笔裙和连裤袜去普拉特学院。

838
00:34:52.080 --> 00:34:52.760
Really?
真的吗？

839
00:34:53.080 --> 00:34:53.560
Really.
真的。

840
00:34:53.800 --> 00:34:55.800
Pam, I hope there's parking.
帕姆，希望那儿有停车位。

841
00:34:56.260 --> 00:35:02.780
Well, listen, I wanted you to know, Randy Cordray shared that this parking lot scene took place
听着，我想让你知道，兰迪·科德雷分享说，这场停车场戏是在一个极其炎热的日子里拍摄的。

842
00:35:02.780 --> 00:35:04.240
on an incredibly hot day.
洛杉矶当时气温高达一百多华氏度，史蒂夫本来就怕热，他还得跑着进入这场戏，穿着西装简直热坏了。

843
00:35:04.240 --> 00:35:11.840
It was like triple-digit weather in Los Angeles, and Steve runs hot anyway, and he had to run into
嗯，菲尔·谢伊找来了一件冷却背心，让史蒂夫穿在西装里面帮他降温。

844
00:35:11.840 --> 00:35:14.460
this scene, and it was super hot in a suit.
这是一种马拉松运动员和专业选手会用的背心。

845
00:35:14.930 --> 00:35:22.080
Well, Phil Shea found a cooling vest that Steve could wear under his suit to help keep him cool.
他们用它来降低体温。

846
00:35:22.280 --> 00:35:25.440
It's the type of vest that marathon runners and athletes have.
里面有那种冷冻凝胶包，史蒂夫当时就把它穿在西装里面。

847
00:35:25.620 --> 00:35:27.620
They use it to cool their body temperature down.
我从没听说过这东西，这很正常，因为我永远不会主动去寻找它。

848
00:35:27.800 --> 00:35:32.400
It has these little frozen gel packs, and Steve had that on under his suit.
我永远不会想，我该如何在任何情况下让自己更冷一点？

849
00:35:32.600 --> 00:35:37.800
I've never heard of this thing, which makes sense to me because I would never seek it out.
我从没听说过这东西，这很正常，因为我永远不会主动去寻找它。

850
00:35:38.080 --> 00:35:41.560
I would never think, how can I be colder in any situation?
我永远不会想，我该如何在任何情况下让自己更冷一点？

851
00:35:41.700 --> 00:35:42.160
No, never.
不，从来没有。

852
00:35:42.320 --> 00:35:42.980
It's a whole thing.
这事儿挺复杂的。

853
00:35:44.460 --> 00:35:46.600
Many different types of cooling vests that you can get.
市面上有很多种冷却背心。

854
00:35:46.880 --> 00:35:47.820
Athletes use them.
运动员会用。

855
00:35:48.600 --> 00:35:49.760
Soldiers use them.
士兵也会用。

856
00:35:50.060 --> 00:35:52.260
I mean, you know, it's like a whole thing.
我是说，你知道的，这事儿挺复杂的。

857
00:35:52.460 --> 00:35:53.520
You know what I do own?
你知道我有什么吗？

858
00:35:53.740 --> 00:35:54.020
What?
什么？

859
00:35:54.240 --> 00:35:55.400
A warming veSt.
一件加热背心。

860
00:35:55.680 --> 00:35:59.840
I have a vest, and you put little hot packs in it, and it keeps you warm.
我有一件背心，往里面放些小暖宝宝，就能保持温暖。

861
00:36:00.060 --> 00:36:03.760
I bought it so that I could watch my son play ice hockey outdoors.
我买它是为了能去看我儿子在户外打冰球。

862
00:36:04.200 --> 00:36:04.520
Yeah.
是啊。

863
00:36:04.700 --> 00:36:08.160
Well, we used to stuff those little hot pocket thingies.
以前我们总是塞那些小暖宝宝之类的东西。

864
00:36:08.220 --> 00:36:08.740
What do you call them?
那叫什么来着？

865
00:36:09.180 --> 00:36:10.760
Not the food hot pockets.
不是那种热口袋披萨。

866
00:36:11.260 --> 00:36:12.300
What are they called?
那叫什么？

867
00:36:12.300 --> 00:36:16.120
I love the idea of us having a vest filled with hot pockets, though.
不过我倒是很喜欢我们穿一件塞满热口袋披萨的背心这个主意。

868
00:36:16.300 --> 00:36:19.680
Because then if you get hungry, it's a snack as well.
因为那样如果你饿了，还能当零食吃。

869
00:36:19.860 --> 00:36:21.200
It keeps you warm and full.
既保暖又能填饱肚子。

870
00:36:21.200 --> 00:36:26.060
Listen, on the office, I had one skirt that had two little stitch pockets in the back,
听着，在《办公室》剧组时，我有一条裙子，后面有两个小缝口袋，

871
00:36:26.060 --> 00:36:28.880
and I had one little tiny stitch pocket in the front.
前面还有一个极小的缝口袋。

872
00:36:28.880 --> 00:36:31.380
They would give us those little hot pack things.
他们会给我们发那种小暖宝宝。

873
00:36:31.620 --> 00:36:32.540
Little hand warmers?
暖手宝吗？

874
00:36:32.740 --> 00:36:33.420
Little hand warmers.
就是暖手宝。

875
00:36:33.680 --> 00:36:35.520
I would stick two in my shoes.
我会往鞋里塞两个。

876
00:36:35.540 --> 00:36:38.300
I would stick one in that front pocket, two in my back pocket.
我会往前面的口袋塞一个，后面口袋塞两个。

877
00:36:38.500 --> 00:36:40.060
I'd stick a few in my bra.
我还会往胸罩里塞几个。

878
00:36:40.400 --> 00:36:40.780
Same.
我也是。

879
00:36:40.900 --> 00:36:41.500
Yeah, I remember that.
是啊，我记得。

880
00:36:41.580 --> 00:36:41.740
Yeah.
嗯。

881
00:36:42.020 --> 00:36:44.300
And if my sweater had pockets, I'd stick them in there.
如果我的毛衣有口袋，我也会塞进去。

882
00:36:44.560 --> 00:36:48.280
I'd stick so many of those on my body when we were filming outside when it was cold.
天冷在户外拍摄时，我身上会塞好多那种东西。

883
00:36:48.460 --> 00:36:50.800
One time, our camera operator, Matt Stone, was like,
有一次，我们的摄影师马特·斯通对我说，

884
00:36:50.800 --> 00:36:55.320
Ange, just don't take this the wrong way, but I can see lumps in your butt on camera.
“安吉，别误会，但我能在镜头里看到你屁股上有肿块。”

885
00:36:56.140 --> 00:36:59.200
Like, they don't look human, like human lumps.
“看起来不像人类，不像人类的肿块。”

886
00:36:59.420 --> 00:37:00.420
I was like, dang it.
我说，该死。

887
00:37:00.540 --> 00:37:03.500
And I had to take my little heater things out of my pockets.
然后我不得不把口袋里的小暖宝宝拿出来。

888
00:37:03.740 --> 00:37:07.440
Well, I can't believe that they got a cooling vest, and I'm glad they did.
好吧，真不敢相信他们买了冷却背心，我很高兴他们买了。

889
00:37:07.580 --> 00:37:08.140
I am, too.
我也是。

890
00:37:08.160 --> 00:37:09.480
I thought that was so smart.
我觉得这太聪明了。

891
00:37:09.680 --> 00:37:10.020
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

892
00:37:10.600 --> 00:37:12.440
Well, it's time for another weigh-in.
好了，又到了称重的时间了。

893
00:37:12.620 --> 00:37:13.560
Big announcement.
重大公告。

894
00:37:13.560 --> 00:37:15.280
They lost 31 pounds.
他们减掉了31磅。

895
00:37:15.560 --> 00:37:16.000
Wow.
哇。

896
00:37:16.500 --> 00:37:19.120
Michael and Holly are so excited they're going to do a wrap.
迈克尔和霍莉太兴奋了，他们要来一段说唱。

897
00:37:19.360 --> 00:37:22.940
It's the most adorable thing, because they're so dorky and cute together.
这太可爱了，因为他们在一起时又呆萌又可爱。

898
00:37:23.320 --> 00:37:27.380
Well, a little wrap trivia is that they have about 10 minutes of them wrapping,
关于这段说唱有个小花絮，他们录了大约10分钟的说唱，

899
00:37:27.600 --> 00:37:32.000
even though the part that you see in the show was completely scripted,
尽管你在节目中看到的那部分是完全照着剧本演的，

900
00:37:32.540 --> 00:37:35.640
even down to Holly, like, rubbing her jacket.
甚至连霍莉摩擦她夹克的动作都写在剧本里。

901
00:37:35.780 --> 00:37:36.140
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

902
00:37:36.200 --> 00:37:37.000
The wicky, wicky, what?
那个什么什么，什么来着？

903
00:37:37.100 --> 00:37:38.060
All of that was scripted.
那一切都是写好的剧本。

904
00:37:38.100 --> 00:37:39.940
All of that was scripted, but they did go,
那一切都是剧本，但他们确实，

905
00:37:40.020 --> 00:37:44.740
on and on, and Amy Ryan gave an interview where she said this was her favorite scene
没完没了地演，艾米·瑞恩在一次采访中说这是她最喜欢的一场戏，

906
00:37:44.740 --> 00:37:46.700
to shoot because they had so much fun.
因为拍的时候太开心了。

907
00:37:46.900 --> 00:37:48.420
The crew said the same thing.
剧组人员也这么说。

908
00:37:48.580 --> 00:37:53.540
They said it was so much fun that those two just went off, and that the chemistry was
他们说那场戏太好玩了，那两人完全即兴发挥，而且那种化学反应，

909
00:37:53.540 --> 00:37:54.360
just so apparent.
简直显而易见。

910
00:37:54.540 --> 00:38:00.980
I think this was the scene when they were shooting when they realized, oh, yeah, these two.
我觉得这就是他们拍摄时意识到，哦，没错，就是这两人。

911
00:38:01.240 --> 00:38:01.780
True love.
真爱。

912
00:38:01.980 --> 00:38:02.220
Yeah.
没错。

913
00:38:02.620 --> 00:38:06.980
Well, now it's week three, and there is a new receptionist in town.
好了，现在是第三周了，城里来了一位新前台。

914
00:38:07.360 --> 00:38:08.560
Yes, Ronnie.
没错，罗尼。

915
00:38:08.560 --> 00:38:11.460
Yeah, Ronnie, played by Dale Raul.
对，罗尼，由戴尔·劳尔饰演。

916
00:38:11.820 --> 00:38:13.380
She has been in a ton of stuff.
她演过很多作品。

917
00:38:13.520 --> 00:38:15.080
She was Maxine in True Blood.
她在《真爱如血》里演玛克辛。

918
00:38:15.320 --> 00:38:16.700
Oh, Maxine Fortenberry.
哦，玛克辛·福滕伯里。

919
00:38:16.700 --> 00:38:17.880
I love True Blood.
我超爱《真爱如血》。

920
00:38:18.100 --> 00:38:19.060
She was fantastic.
她演得太棒了。

921
00:38:19.400 --> 00:38:20.640
Of course, you would know that.
你当然会知道这个。

922
00:38:20.780 --> 00:38:21.060
Yes.
是的。

923
00:38:21.220 --> 00:38:23.220
I have a crossover connection with Dale.
我和戴尔还有过交集。

924
00:38:23.500 --> 00:38:23.940
Tell me.
快告诉我。

925
00:38:24.140 --> 00:38:26.240
We were both on Fresh Off the Boat.
我们都演过《初来乍到》。

926
00:38:26.560 --> 00:38:27.360
Well, there you go.
原来如此。

927
00:38:27.520 --> 00:38:30.880
Not Monk, surprisingly, but Fresh Off the Boat.
令人惊讶的是不是《神探阿蒙》，而是《初来乍到》。

928
00:38:30.980 --> 00:38:32.800
Well, she will come back in season six.
好吧，她会在第六季回归。

929
00:38:32.800 --> 00:38:35.440
This is not the last we're going to see of Ronnie.
我们还会再见到罗尼的。

930
00:38:36.060 --> 00:38:39.580
Meanwhile, we're going to see Pam in her first class.
与此同时，我们要看帕姆去上她的第一节课了。

931
00:38:39.780 --> 00:38:41.040
She looks so cute.
她看起来真可爱。

932
00:38:41.260 --> 00:38:43.660
She has, like, I'm calling it the college ponytail.
她扎了个，我管它叫大学马尾辫。

933
00:38:43.960 --> 00:38:46.420
She wears this really cute ponytail at school.
她在学校里扎着这个超级可爱的马尾辫。

934
00:38:46.700 --> 00:38:47.120
All right.
好吧。

935
00:38:47.220 --> 00:38:50.020
The ponytail is the only thing that's cute about Pam.
马尾辫是帕姆身上唯一可爱的地方了。

936
00:38:50.280 --> 00:38:50.960
Are you kidding?
你开什么玩笑？

937
00:38:50.980 --> 00:38:53.660
I thought you looked so cute in all of your college scenes.
我觉得你在所有大学场景里看起来都特别可爱。

938
00:38:54.040 --> 00:38:57.220
Did you notice how young everyone else is in the class?
你注意到班里其他人有多年轻了吗？

939
00:38:57.220 --> 00:38:58.380
Oh, you stop it.
哦，你快闭嘴吧。

940
00:38:58.480 --> 00:39:00.220
No, but this was a deliberate choice.
不，但这绝对是刻意安排的。

941
00:39:00.460 --> 00:39:01.060
Well, okay.
好吧，行吧。

942
00:39:01.500 --> 00:39:03.120
Pam is in her late 20s.
帕姆已经快三十岁了。

943
00:39:03.120 --> 00:39:05.760
Do you like how immediately I, like, stand up for my best friend?
你喜欢我这种立刻站出来维护我闺蜜的样子吗？

944
00:39:05.760 --> 00:39:06.860
I'm like, you stop it.
我就像是在说，你快闭嘴吧。

945
00:39:06.900 --> 00:39:07.840
You are beautiful.
你很漂亮。

946
00:39:08.160 --> 00:39:10.560
You look just as young as those other ones.
你看上去和那些人一样年轻。

947
00:39:10.680 --> 00:39:10.760
That's right.
没错。

948
00:39:10.760 --> 00:39:12.120
And you are smart.
而且你很聪明。

949
00:39:12.680 --> 00:39:12.960
Okay.
好吧。

950
00:39:12.960 --> 00:39:13.420
Thank you.
谢谢你。

951
00:39:13.580 --> 00:39:13.960
You're welcome.
不客气。

952
00:39:14.240 --> 00:39:16.920
I want you to know I was not being down on myself.
我想让你知道，我并不是在贬低自己。

953
00:39:17.080 --> 00:39:20.340
I was just pointing out a deliberate production choice.
我只是指出了一个刻意的制作选择。

954
00:39:20.920 --> 00:39:25.280
Pam is in her late 20s, and they made sure that everyone in this class,
帕姆快三十岁了，而他们确保了班上的每个人，

955
00:39:25.280 --> 00:39:27.620
that the background performers were all much younger.
那些背景演员都年轻得多。

956
00:39:27.820 --> 00:39:29.700
They're just starting off in college, right?
他们才刚上大学，对吧？

957
00:39:29.880 --> 00:39:31.180
Pam's going back to school.
帕姆是重返校园。

958
00:39:31.320 --> 00:39:36.520
And they did want to create this story for Pam that she is kind of, you know.
他们确实想为帕姆创造这样一个故事，让她显得，你知道的。

959
00:39:37.520 --> 00:39:38.000
Yeah.
